{
  "manufacturer": "Daikin",
  "manufacturer_slug": "daikin",
  "model": "EKRHH Daikin HomeHub (Modbus TCP/RTU for Daikin Altherma and air-to-air heat pumps)",
  "model_slug": "ekrhh-homehub",
  "short_model": "Daikin EKRHH HomeHub",
  "aliases": [
    "EKRHH",
    "Daikin HomeHub",
    "4P744838-1E",
    "Daikin Altherma 3 Modbus",
    "Altherma Smart Grid Modbus"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Heat pump (air-to-water) Modbus interface",
  "applies_to": "Daikin HomeHub EKRHH in use case 3 (Modbus for Daikin Altherma air-to-water heat pumps) and use case 4 (Modbus smart-grid control of air-to-air heat pumps), installer reference guide 4P744838-1E (2026.01).",
  "summary": "The Daikin HomeHub (EKRHH) connects to a Daikin Altherma system and offers a Modbus TCP (port 502, or 802 with TLS) or Modbus RTU slave. Holding registers set leaving-water and room setpoints, operation mode, on/off, quiet mode, hot-water reheat and booster, weather-dependent mode and the smart-grid mode with power limits; input registers return error state and code, pump/compressor/heater/defrost states, water, outdoor and refrigerant temperatures, flow, power use and setpoint limits. For air-to-air units only the smart-grid mode and demand-control power limit are offered.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide lists register offsets 1-based and says PDU addressing is 0-based: register 1 is requested at PDU address 0. Every wire address here is the printed offset minus one."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Installer reference guide - Daikin HomeHub EKRHH",
    "doc_number": "4P744838-1E",
    "revision_date": "2026-01",
    "url": "https://www.daikin.eu/content/dam/document-library/Installer-reference-guide/heat/accessories/ekrhh/EKRHH_Installer%20reference%20guide_4PEN744838-1E_English.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 39-44 use case 3 (protocol, data types, holding and input registers, special values); pp. 45-47 smart grid buffering; pp. 48-51 use case 4"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Data types are Daikin's: Temp16 and Pow16 are signed 16-bit values divided by 100 (°C and kW); Int16 is a signed 16-bit value with no scaling; Text16 is two ASCII characters. The holding-register setpoints are printed as Int16, so they are whole degrees.",
    "Holding offsets 59 and 61 (thermostat inputs): with external room thermostat control ([C-07]=1) they are only valid when thermostat type [C-05]=0 (SW contact), otherwise they read 0 (off). Not available on Daikin Altherma 3 R / 3 M units with Micon ID 20002203.",
    "Offsets 1001 and 1002 belong to use case 4 (air-to-air heat pumps) and are the only registers supported there. The type of 1001 is not printed; it is listed as INT16 with the same codes as offset 56.",
    "Special return values: 32767 = register unsupported, 32766 = register unavailable in this configuration, 32765 = value not loaded yet (also returned while the HomeHub synchronises).",
    "Writes to setpoint registers outside the configured range are clamped to the nearest limit; out-of-range writes to other registers are ignored."
  ],
